@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:architecture;release] mila-apple-native-standalone
The Apple native package MUST build and test as a standalone Swift package without importing or
invoking alternate UI runtime; its release verification MUST use the package's Swift toolchain and typed Rust
FFI seam.


@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:architecture] mila-apple-host-app-entry-only
The `App` host package MUST contain only the process entry point and bundle
metadata. Behaviour, strings and authority checks belong to `MilaNativeUI`
and the Rust FFI, so the app and the package tests exercise the same code.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:release] mila-apple-both-platforms-build
Continuous integration MUST build the app for an iOS target as well as macOS.
`swift test` compiles only the macOS slice and cannot catch iOS-only
compile failures.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:release;security] mila-apple-release-signing
`mila-build <ios|macos> release` MUST refuse a missing team, signing identity,
provisioning profile, version or (macOS) notary profile; MUST refuse a profile
whose team or application identifier is not this team's `dev.overalls.mila`;
MUST NOT fall back to ad-hoc signing; and MUST verify the artifact's signature,
signing team and (macOS) notarization before reporting success.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:localization;release] mila-apple-bundled-catalogs
Every Apple build and package test MUST first generate
`Sources/MilaNativeUI/Resources` from the shared ARB catalogs with
`mila/localization/generate_catalogs.py`, one bundle per supported locale, so
every locale ships and no stale copy is committed. Every `MilaMessage` MUST
resolve through an existing shared catalog identity rather than an Apple-only
string, and a supported non-English locale MUST render its own catalog form.
